[
    {
        "content": "<p>To what extent can I use just the natural deduction rules including those for predicate logic and equality in a forward reasoning approach without tactics? I have only a weak understanding of type theory, so I'm not certain exactly what the correspondence of these rules would be to the type theory proof terms, and what would need to be used beyond these rules for things like definitions and induction. I'm picturing a list of numbered rule applications, where each line gives the rule used, the line numbers of the previous steps needed for the rule to work, and the result of applying the rule.</p>",
        "id": 600797868,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780707651
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That's <code>have</code> statements, available in term mode as well. The used rule is an application in the have's right-hand side, back references are given as variable names instead of indices, and the result is the optional type annotation</p>",
        "id": 600826303,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1780729238
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do you know what the proof terms would be for each of the rules? That is, how could I use each of the rules without tactics?</p>",
        "id": 600923908,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780787236
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.elim#doc\">docs#Or.elim</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.inl#doc\">docs#Or.inl</a> <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.inr#doc\">docs#Or.inr</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.left#doc\">docs#And.left</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.right#doc\">docs#And.right</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.intro#doc\">docs#And.intro</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.mp#doc\">docs#Iff.mp</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.mpr#doc\">docs#Iff.mpr</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.intro#doc\">docs#Iff.intro</a>. For implication introduction for <code>p → q</code>, that's <code>fun hp ↦ ...</code> where <code>hp</code> is an arbitrary name and <code>...</code> is a term of type <code>q</code>. Likewise for implication elimination this is just function application, so given <code>f : p → q</code> and <code>hp : p</code>, one has <code>f hp : q</code>. <code>¬ p := p → false</code> is a definitional equality in Lean, so the negation elimination and introduction rules are just special cases of implication. Finally, there's <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=True.intro#doc\">docs#True.intro</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=False.elim#doc\">docs#False.elim</a>.</p>",
        "id": 600927463,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780788209
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably <a href=\"https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/\">#tpil</a> has a lot of examples of what you're looking for in the early chapters.</p>",
        "id": 600927627,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780788255
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>e.g., <a href=\"https://leanprover.github.io/theorem_proving_in_lean4/Propositions-and-Proofs/#propositions-and-proofs\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 600927993,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780788353
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are there ones for the introduction and elimination rules for the predicate logic (forall, exists, eq)?</p>",
        "id": 600929590,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780788792
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The introduction and elimination rules for forall are the same as for implication. To get a <code>∀ x, p x</code> you can do <code>fun x =&gt; ...</code> where <code>x</code> is an arbitrary name and <code>...</code> is a term of type <code>p x</code>, and if you have a <code>f : ∀ x : α, p x</code> and a <code>c : α</code> then <code>f c : p c</code>.</p>",
        "id": 600930344,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780788998
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The introduction rule for <code>Exists</code> is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Exists.intro#doc\">docs#Exists.intro</a> and the elimination rule is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Exists.elim#doc\">docs#Exists.elim</a>.</p>",
        "id": 600930427,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780789018
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What is <code>p</code>? Would you happen to have an example?</p>",
        "id": 600931986,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780789430
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>p</code> is a placeholder for a predicate. For example, in this snippet <code>p x := x = c</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">he</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exists</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hc</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">he</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600933047,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780789720
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So in the forall case, <code>p x</code> is the application of <code>x</code> to the predicate function <code>p</code>?</p>",
        "id": 600933673,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780790072
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you.</p>",
        "id": 600933783,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1780790161
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a way to take a proof done with tactics and automatically construct a forward proof that uses just these rules?</p>",
        "id": 602712263,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1781317328
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a tactic that will construct the shortest proof of a propositional formula using just <code>intro</code>, <code>exact</code>, and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.elim#doc\">docs#Or.elim</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.inl#doc\">docs#Or.inl</a> <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Or.inr#doc\">docs#Or.inr</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.left#doc\">docs#And.left</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.right#doc\">docs#And.right</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=And.intro#doc\">docs#And.intro</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.mp#doc\">docs#Iff.mp</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.mpr#doc\">docs#Iff.mpr</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Iff.intro#doc\">docs#Iff.intro</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=True.intro#doc\">docs#True.intro</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=False.elim#doc\">docs#False.elim</a>?</p>",
        "id": 602733733,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1781325186
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you may be interested in <a href=\"https://github.com/chasenorman/CanonicalLean\">canonical</a></p>",
        "id": 602735360,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1781325682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That looks interesting. I tried adding it and get<br>\n<code>/home/pthomas/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.31.0-rc1/bin/lake setup-file /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/TtfpLean/UTLC/Term.lean -</code> failed:</p>\n<p>stderr:<br>\n✖ [95/116] Building Canonical.Monomorphize.Basic (1.4s)<br>\ntrace: .&gt; LEAN_PATH=/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Cli/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/batteries/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Qq/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/aesop/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/proofwidgets/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/importGraph/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/LeanSearchClient/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/plausible/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/mathlib/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/.lake/build/lib/lean:/home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/build/lib/lean /home/pthomas/.elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.31.0-rc1/bin/lean /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.lean -o /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/.lake/build/lib/lean/Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.olean -i /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/.lake/build/lib/lean/Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.ilean -c /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/.lake/build/ir/Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.c --setup /home/pthomas/Desktop/github/ttfp_lean/.lake/packages/Canonical/.lake/build/ir/Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.setup.json --json<br>\nerror: Canonical/Monomorphize/Basic.lean:319:0: unexpected identifier; expected command<br>\nerror: Lean exited with code 1<br>\nSome required targets logged failures:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Canonical.Monomorphize.Basic<br>\nFailed to build module dependencies.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 602739998,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1781327087
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"ttfp_lean\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">version</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"0.1.0\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">keywords</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"math\"</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">defaultTargets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"TtfpLean\"</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">leanOptions</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unicode</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pretty</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">prints</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span>\n<span class=\"n\">relaxedAutoImplicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"n\">weak</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mathlibStandardSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">maxSynthPendingDepth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"mathlib\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"leanprover-community\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"v4.31.0-rc1\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Canonical\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"chasenorman\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">lean_lib</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"TtfpLean\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 602740470,
