    {
        "content": "<p>I think you just need to go back to an earlier version</p>",
        "id": 602800694,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781347641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If I change it to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Canonical\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"chasenorman\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"v4.30.0\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I get the same error.</p>",
        "id": 602882180,
        "sender_full_name": "Paige Thomas",
        "timestamp": 1781374326
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I mean you need to set your <code>lean-toolchain</code> and the version you take mathlib from. So maybe try</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"o\">[[</span><span class=\"n\">require</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"mathlib\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">scope</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"leanprover-community\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"v4.30.0\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and <code>leanprover/lean4:v4.30.0</code> in your lean-toolchain file.</p>",
        "id": 602882474,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1781374432
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yep, that fixed it. Thank you!</p>",
